1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,510
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,510 --> 00:00:05,230
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:06,380
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:07,650
I've been a labor and
delivery

5
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:09,050
nurse for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:10,500
On my feet all night,

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,450
bending over the bed for
hours.

8
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:13,380
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:14,810
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:16,960
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:18,930
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:20,780
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:21,790
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:23,060
This is different.

15
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:23,910
Tight.

16
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:24,720
Full.

17
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:25,710
Like a band around

18
00:00:25,710 --> 00:00:27,650
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:29,010
And for two years I've

20
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:30,470
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:31,610
Give it time.

22
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,130
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:35,580
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,420
At three months,

25
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:38,360
give it six.

26
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,430
At six months,

27
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:41,140
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,020
At a year,

29
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:44,210
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,520
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:46,850
We went down the list.

32
00:00:46,890 --> 00:00:48,740
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:48,790 --> 00:00:50,500
Every session,

34
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,070
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,330
I got stronger.

36
00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:54,740
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:55,970
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:55,970 --> 00:00:57,240
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,250
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:00,390
and nobody could tell me

41
00:01:00,390 --> 00:01:01,430
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:01,470 --> 00:01:02,960
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,930
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,760
And after that, a second

45
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:08,460
operation to go back in

46
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,510
and do it over.

47
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,190
I said no.

48
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,070
Every evening I stepped
out

49
00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:14,590
of the car at the hospital

50
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:16,030
and my knee felt like a
band

51
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:19,530
was wrapped around it,
tightening every inch

52
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:20,910
I tried to straighten.

53
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:22,910
Every evening I took
something

54
00:01:22,910 --> 00:01:24,930
for it and went to my
shift.

55
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,370
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:27,500
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,290
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:29,290 --> 00:01:30,700
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

59
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:32,940
game without shifting
every two minutes.

60
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:33,880
At work,

61
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,160
I'd kneel by the bed to
coach

62
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:36,620
a mom through a push,

63
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:37,490
then need the rail

64
00:01:37,490 --> 00:01:38,510
to get back up.

65
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,130
Thirty years of helping
babies

66
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:41,150
into the world,

67
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:42,090
and I was the one

68
00:01:42,090 --> 00:01:43,320
who needed a hand up.

69
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,720
It woke me at night,

70
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,500
and it turned ordinary
things,

71
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:47,590
like getting in the car

72
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:48,920
or up off the couch,

73
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,100
into a decision.

74
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,110
After a long and serious

75
00:01:52,110 --> 00:01:53,440
talk with my husband,

76
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:55,300
I went back in one more
time.

77
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:56,540
That was the fourth set

78
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:58,080
of X-rays on this knee.

79
00:01:58,150 --> 00:01:59,740
And like the three before
it,

80
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:02,220
the answer was everything
looks great.

81
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:04,130
No loosening, no
infection,

82
00:02:04,130 --> 00:02:05,140
nothing wrong.

83
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:06,180
Only this time there

84
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:07,380
was no new number.

85
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:09,680
Nobody said give it
another six months.

86
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,780
There was nothing left to
give it.

87
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:12,740
I sat in the parking

88
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:13,800
lot for a while.

89
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:15,660
Okay, I thought.

90
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,060
Then explain this.

91
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:19,470
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

92
00:02:19,470 --> 00:02:20,940
I hit my breaking point.

93
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:23,340
It was around 2:30 in the
morning,

94
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:24,420
on a night off.

95
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:26,970
Everyone in the house was
asleep

96
00:02:26,970 --> 00:02:28,740
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

97
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:29,920
with my leg up,

98
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,590
trying to find any angle
where

99
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:33,440
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

100
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:35,200
around my knee and
tightening.

101
00:02:35,270 --> 00:02:37,690
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

102
00:02:37,810 --> 00:02:39,840
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

103
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:41,040
And I just thought,

104
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,730
is this really my life
now?

105
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,350
I can't live like this.

106
00:02:44,950 --> 00:02:46,920
So I made myself a
promise.

107
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:47,850
I wouldn't go a day

108
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:49,490
without looking for an
answer.

109
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:51,030
And when I found one,

110
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:52,350
I'd share it with everyone

111
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:53,910
going through the same
thing.

112
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:56,260
So I got my laptop out

113
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:57,290
and went looking.

114
00:02:57,470 --> 00:02:58,720
Not for a product.

115
00:02:59,290 --> 00:03:00,570
For an explanation.

116
00:03:00,810 --> 00:03:02,650
Mayo Clinic forums,

117
00:03:02,650 --> 00:03:04,940
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

118
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:07,550
doctor videos, medical
animations.

119
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:09,410
And that's when I found a
video

120
00:03:09,410 --> 00:03:11,470
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

121
00:03:11,510 --> 00:03:12,980
Steven Salinger,

122
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:14,100
whose own wife

123
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:16,120
had been through exactly
this.

124
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,210
But before I say anything
else,

125
00:03:18,210 --> 00:03:19,890
I want to be straight with
you.

126
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:22,720
You've already had
something work fast.

127
00:03:22,790 --> 00:03:23,730
The ice.

128
00:03:23,830 --> 00:03:25,620
The first week of a new
pill.

129
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,430
The good day after a
session.

130
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,320
Then it wore off.

131
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:31,630
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

132
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:33,350
Fast relief isn't relief.

133
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:34,540
It's a preview.

134
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:36,730
So I'm not going to tell

135
00:03:36,730 --> 00:03:38,030
you this works fast.

136
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:38,940
It doesn't.

137
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:41,190
But if you're willing to
be patient,

138
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:42,070
and to look at what's

139
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:43,630
going on around your new
knee

140
00:03:43,630 --> 00:03:45,270
instead of inside it,
there

141
00:03:45,270 --> 00:03:47,590
is a real reason it still
hurts.

142
00:03:47,770 --> 00:03:49,590
And something you can do
about it.

143
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,110
Let me explain what he
said,

144
00:03:52,110 --> 00:03:53,280
because this is what
changed

145
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,630
everything for me.

146
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:56,920
He started with the
basics.

147
00:03:57,210 --> 00:03:58,720
A knee replacement takes
out

148
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,510
the worn joint surfaces

149
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:02,500
and puts in metal and
plastic.

150
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:04,330
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

151
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:06,110
you had before the
operation.

152
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:08,410
That part I already knew.

153
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:09,820
But then he explained
something

154
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:11,310
nobody had ever told me.

155
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:12,160
He said,

156
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,310
think about a swollen foot

157
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:14,360
inside a shoe.

158
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:15,760
The shoe didn't shrink.

159
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,770
Your foot is taking up
more room,

160
00:04:17,770 --> 00:04:19,160
so everything feels
cramped

161
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,670
and tight and squeezed.

162
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,430
Your new knee sits

163
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:23,930
in a limited space

164
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:26,340
with living tissue packed
all around it.

165
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:28,570
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

166
00:04:28,570 --> 00:04:30,340
had to work through that
tissue.

167
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:32,940
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

168
00:04:33,050 --> 00:04:34,780
At first that's normal.

169
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:36,520
But in some people that
swelling can

170
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:39,080
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

171
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,980
And swollen tissue takes
up more

172
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:42,820
room than calm tissue
does.

173
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,240
So when you bend,

174
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,270
that tissue gets
compressed.

175
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,440
When you straighten,

176
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:49,670
it gets pulled tight.

177
00:04:49,710 --> 00:04:50,700
That's the band.

178
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:53,060
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

179
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:53,940
And you start being

180
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:55,630
the one who says,

181
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:56,730
you go ahead.

182
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:57,890
I'll stay here.

183
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:59,490
And that's exactly why so
much

184
00:04:59,490 --> 00:05:01,200
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

185
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:03,300
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

186
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,190
around the knee.

187
00:05:04,230 --> 00:05:05,130
Worth doing,

188
00:05:05,130 --> 00:05:06,110
and I'd done it.

189
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,840
It does nothing about
tissue

190
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:08,980
taking up room.

191
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:11,100
A nerve block quiets the
nerve

192
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,400
carrying the signal.

193
00:05:12,530 --> 00:05:14,920
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

194
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:16,950
But when that irritated
tissue

195
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:18,400
finally calms down,

196
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,870
it holds less fluid,

197
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:21,410
and it takes up less room.

198
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:24,320
Less room taken up means
less pressure

199
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:25,820
squeezing the joint.

200
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:27,730
That's what takes the
pressure off.

201
00:05:27,810 --> 00:05:29,410
After two years of this,

202
00:05:29,410 --> 00:05:30,940
it finally made sense.

203
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:33,450
The problem was never the
new knee.

204
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:35,440
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

205
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,010
He calls it the squeeze.

206
00:05:37,050 --> 00:05:39,260
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

207
00:05:39,350 --> 00:05:40,880
I'd bought knee sleeves,

208
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:43,410
compression socks,
compression braces,

209
00:05:43,410 --> 00:05:45,630
creams, half of Amazon
really,

210
00:05:45,630 --> 00:05:47,220
and all any of it gave me

211
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:48,090
was an hour.

212
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:49,130
I even looked at going

213
00:05:49,130 --> 00:05:50,930
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

214
00:05:51,090 --> 00:05:52,600
But at $200 a session

215
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,620
with nothing covered by
insurance,

216
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:55,940
that was a quick no.

217
00:05:56,390 --> 00:05:57,360
Then one night

218
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,050
I went back to that knee
replacement

219
00:05:59,050 --> 00:06:00,640
group and actually read
it.

220
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,100
Thousands of people,

221
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:03,800
years out from surgery,

222
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:06,030
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

223
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:07,490
nobody could explain.

224
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,720
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

225
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:11,920
the same thing kept coming
up.

226
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,480
This one device,

227
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:14,610
and people saying

228
00:06:14,610 --> 00:06:15,840
it was the first thing

229
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,080
that made a difference.

230
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:19,630
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:20,750
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:22,050
she's selling me
something,

233
00:06:22,050 --> 00:06:23,740
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:25,640
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,640
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:28,560
that if I ever found

237
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,700
something that helped,

238
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:30,740
I'd say so.

239
00:06:31,290 --> 00:06:32,810
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:34,100
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:34,170 --> 00:06:36,400
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,970
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

243
00:06:37,970 --> 00:06:39,960
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

244
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:41,930
But I went to their
website anyway,

245
00:06:41,930 --> 00:06:42,710
just to see what all

246
00:06:42,710 --> 00:06:43,910
the fuss was about.

247
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,950
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

248
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:48,420
charge $200 a session for,

249
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:51,190
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:51,190 --> 00:06:52,180
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:53,600
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:53,690 --> 00:06:55,400
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:55,530 --> 00:06:57,450
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:57,450 --> 00:07:00,100
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:02,280
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:03,810
Four strength levels.

257
00:07:03,850 --> 00:07:05,800
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:07,450
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:07:07,570 --> 00:07:08,880
Ninety days.

260
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:10,790
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:13,230
no questions, no store
credit,

262
00:07:13,230 --> 00:07:14,880
and you don't even send it
back.

263
00:07:15,450 --> 00:07:17,730
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

264
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:19,330
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:19,450 --> 00:07:20,850
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:20,850 --> 00:07:22,000
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,660
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:23,790 --> 00:07:25,280
Only the right knee was
replaced,

269
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,290
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

270
00:07:27,290 --> 00:07:28,100
and I'd done it through

271
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:29,760
every shift for two years.

272
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,720
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:32,760
When it came,

274
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,820
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:35,950
because I'd been let down

276
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:37,690
too many times to get
excited.

277
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:40,580
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:42,640
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:44,330
More like it was coming
from inside

280
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:46,350
the knee and spreading
around it.

281
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:47,610
And that was it.

282
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,270
That was the whole
experience.

283
00:07:49,430 --> 00:07:50,600
When I took it off,

284
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,570
I'll be honest,

285
00:07:51,570 --> 00:07:53,270
nothing dramatic had
happened.

286
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:55,110
And after what that video
said,

287
00:07:55,110 --> 00:07:56,910
that's exactly what I
expected.

288
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:57,820
What was different

289
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,810
was that for the first

290
00:07:58,810 --> 00:08:00,340
time in two years

291
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:02,200
I'd done something for my
knee

292
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,490
instead of to it.

293
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:04,340
Twenty minutes,

294
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:05,400
in my own chair,

295
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,570
after my shift.

296
00:08:06,630 --> 00:08:08,690
No drive, no copay.

297
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:10,070
They say twenty minutes.

298
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:11,150
I did thirty,

299
00:08:11,150 --> 00:08:12,870
twice a day,

300
00:08:12,870 --> 00:08:14,640
lowest setting that first
week.

301
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:15,930
Once when I got home,

302
00:08:15,930 --> 00:08:17,360
once before my shift.

303
00:08:17,470 --> 00:08:18,280
The first week,

304
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:18,990
I couldn't have told

305
00:08:18,990 --> 00:08:20,550
you if anything was
happening.

306
00:08:20,690 --> 00:08:21,450
I tried not to get

307
00:08:21,450 --> 00:08:22,350
my hopes up.

308
00:08:22,530 --> 00:08:23,320
I'd had things help

309
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,940
for a week and then stop.

310
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:26,470
But somewhere in the
second week

311
00:08:26,470 --> 00:08:27,540
I noticed I'd come down

312
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:29,560
the stairs without holding
the rail.

313
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,200
I hadn't decided to.

314
00:08:31,270 --> 00:08:32,710
I just did it, then
stopped

315
00:08:32,710 --> 00:08:34,860
halfway down because I
realized.

316
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:35,930
By the end of the fourth

317
00:08:35,930 --> 00:08:36,860
week I'd slept through

318
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:38,400
the night four times
running.

319
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,940
I stood at the counter and
finished

320
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:41,940
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

321
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,140
None of that is dramatic.

322
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:44,990
All of it was gone

323
00:08:44,990 --> 00:08:46,100
for two years.

324
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:47,790
A few weeks later my
husband asked

325
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:48,590
if I wanted to walk

326
00:08:48,590 --> 00:08:50,140
the long way around the
block.

327
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,140
And for the first time

328
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:51,920
in two years,

329
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,010
I said yes.

330
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,450
I wanted to understand
why,

331
00:08:55,450 --> 00:08:56,810
so I read the whole thing.

332
00:08:56,850 --> 00:08:58,680
It comes down to four
steps.

333
00:08:58,730 --> 00:08:59,430
One.

334
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:00,920
The tissue around a new
knee can

335
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:03,710
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

336
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:04,960
Two.

337
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,310
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

338
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:08,160
so it takes up more

339
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:09,240
room than it should.

340
00:09:09,390 --> 00:09:10,090
Three.

341
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:11,960
There's only so much room
in there.

342
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,430
Bending compresses it.

343
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:15,320
Straightening pulls it
tight.

344
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,760
That's the squeeze.

345
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:18,010
Four.

346
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:20,450
Red and near-infrared
light have been

347
00:09:20,450 --> 00:09:22,740
studied for calming that
inflammation,

348
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:24,110
so the swelling and the
pressure

349
00:09:24,110 --> 00:09:25,440
can come down with it.

350
00:09:25,590 --> 00:09:27,250
In a randomized trial,

351
00:09:27,250 --> 00:09:29,030
patients given light
therapy after

352
00:09:29,030 --> 00:09:30,260
a knee replacement

353
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:32,670
had less pain, less
swelling

354
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:34,060
and better early movement
than

355
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:35,150
those who weren't.

356
00:09:35,190 --> 00:09:37,830
A 2025 review said the
same,

357
00:09:37,830 --> 00:09:39,110
and was clear the evidence

358
00:09:39,110 --> 00:09:40,360
is still limited.

359
00:09:40,430 --> 00:09:42,140
I probably sound like a
broken record

360
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,520
to my family and the other

361
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,990
nurses on my unit.

362
00:09:45,090 --> 00:09:47,190
But after two years of
doing everything

363
00:09:47,190 --> 00:09:49,010
I was told and getting
nowhere,

364
00:09:49,010 --> 00:09:50,160
you have no idea what it's

365
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,540
like to sleep through the
night,

366
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:52,850
say yes to the walk,

367
00:09:52,850 --> 00:09:54,130
and get my life back.

368
00:09:54,810 --> 00:09:56,470
So take it from me.

369
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:57,990
Don't spend another year
waiting

370
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:59,090
for it to settle.

371
00:09:59,190 --> 00:10:01,080
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

372
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:02,610
More than ten thousand
people

373
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:03,660
with pain after a knee

374
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:05,680
replacement have already
tried this.

375
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,320
Some had it worse than I
did.

376
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,440
You can get the KenRelief

377
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,840
wrap from their website,

378
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,830
with a discount link

379
00:10:10,830 --> 00:10:12,510
